   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to the automatic voter\nregistration process",
    "basePrintNo": "S2076",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2076-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Art 5 Title 9, §5-308, El L (as proposed in S.8806 & A.8280-C)",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2076\n\nSPONSOR: GIANARIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to the automatic voter\nregistration process\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to amend the effective date of Chapter 350 of\nthe Laws of 2020.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 makes technical and substantive amendments to Chapter 350 of\nthe Laws of 2020. All participating agencies other than the Department\nof Motor Vehicles will start participating in automatic voter registra-\ntion on January 1, 2024. The State University of New York, will become\nan agency participating in automatic voter registration on January 1,\n2025. Technical amendments include clarification of language that will\nbe utilized on integrated voter registration forms and making language\ngender neutral.\n\nSection 2 makes further technical and substantive amendments to Chapter\n350 of the Laws of 2020 with regard to the mailing of notices sent to\nvoters who have registered through automatic voter registration but did\nnot enroll in a political party.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:  Chapter 350 of the Laws of 2020 created a system of\nautomatic voter registration and pre-registration. As established in the\nchapter, participating agencies provide personal voter registration\napplications that have been integrated with applications for agency\nservices including, amongst other things, name or address changes.  The\nintegrated personal voter registration application shall be available by\npaper or electronically. Modern methods of voter registration, including\nautomatic voter registration, removes barriers to the voting systems and\nwill help New York improve voter turnout.\n\nThis bill makes technical and substantive amendments to the original\nchapter in order to improve the automatic voter registration process and\nallow for timely compliance from participating agencies.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNot yet determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2020 amending the election law relating to estab-\nlishing an automatic voter registration process integrated within desig-\nnated agency applications, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS.8806 and A.8280-C, takes effect.\n",
